{"learnerLanguage":"pt","spokenSeconds":240,"turns":[{"speaker":"character","text":"Good afternoon. My name is James. Could you tell me your full name?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Sure, it's Beatriz Souza."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Let's talk about work. Do you work or are you a student?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I work as data analyst for a logistics company in São Paulo. It's quite demanding, but I genuinely enjoy the problem-solving side of it, especially when a messy dataset finally starts to make sense."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Would you like to change anything about your job?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"Honestly, I'd cut down on the meetings. A lot of them could easily have been an email, and they tend to eat into the time I'd rather spend on, um, deep work."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Describe a skill you learned that took a long time. Say what the skill was, why you learned it, how long it took, and explain how you feel about it now."},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I'd like to talk about learning the cello, which I took up in my mid-twenties. I'd always been drawn to its sound, and after a fairly stressful year I decided I needed something that had nothing to do with screens. It took me around three years to feel even remotely comfortable, mainly because the intonation is so unforgiving, there are no frets to tell you where the notes are. Looking back, I'm really proud I stuck with it, because it taught me to be patient with slow progress, which has spilled over into other areas of my life."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Why do you think adults often give up on learning new skills?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"I think it's largely a matter of expectations. Adults are used to being competent, so the beginner phase feels almost humiliating. On top of that, there's the practical issue of time: once you have a job and a family, the practice is the first thing to go."},{"speaker":"character","text":"Should employers pay for their staff to learn skills unrelated to their job?"},{"speaker":"learner","text":"That's an interesting one. I'd argue it can pay off, since people who are learning something tend to be more engaged overall, although I can see why a small business couldn't justify it. Maybe a middle ground would be a modest allowance that people can spend as they see fit."}],"criteria":[{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"fluencyCoherence","levelBand":null,"name":"Fluency and Coherence","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"lexicalResource","levelBand":null,"name":"Lexical Resource","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"grammar","levelBand":null,"name":"Grammatical Range and Accuracy","scope":"task","sound":false,"voiceOnly":false},{"halfBands":true,"maxBand":9,"minBand":0,"key":"pronunciation","levelBand":null,"name":"Pronunciation","scope":"task","sound":true,"voiceOnly":true}],"task":{"brief":"The test's three parts in a shorter call","minutes":{"max":5,"min":5},"name":"Speaking mock","role":"examiner"},"title":"IELTS Speaking","exam":"ielts"}